# Netlify reads this; Cloudflare Pages reads it too, but *not* for proxying.
#
# There used to be a rule here forwarding /eventdb/* to gencon.eventdb.us, so
# the room dialog could re-check that its events had not moved. It does not work
# on Cloudflare Pages: a `200` rewrite there may only point at paths inside the
# same project, and forwarding to another host is silently ignored — so the
# check reported itself unavailable and nothing said why.
#
# `functions/gencon/[[path]].js` does that job now, which works on Cloudflare
# and is where the one place worth proxying is written down.
